From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:52:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV cache: install_restored_history
 checks the layout in O(spans) (PROTOTYPE)

The live-slot checks of install_restored_history built a dict over every live slot and sorted it,
once per layer and stream. Measured in the ReelCache bridge on A100-40GB (CausVid, 30 layers), this is
134.7 ms of synchronous restore start at 8 chunks, on the critical path of every restore, plain
or overlapped.

_check_restored_layout decides the same conditions from the spans:
- live spans cover exactly [0, local_end), overlaps allowed as before;
- each installed span's first and last slot map as the live layout does, the last span holding a
  slot winning as in the per-slot dict.
Messages are unchanged. A property test compares it with the per-slot check on 3000 random layouts
(gaps, overlaps, negative or out-of-range slots, empty and stray spans) and on replayed layouts.

CPU, 30 layers, CausVid geometry: 40-50 ms -> 0.4 ms at 4 chunks, 110-380 ms -> 1.2 ms at 8.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
